
# Rule 51 —

### Main Rule

> When we talk about a person or thing in a **general sense**, no article is used.

> When a person or thing is **particularised/specified**, an article is used.

### Shortcut:

> **GENERAL → No Article**

> **PARTICULAR → THE**

---

## 1. Man

> **Man is mortal.** ✅

Here **man** means mankind/human beings in general.

Therefore, no article.

---

## 2. Particular Man

> **I saw the man in the forest.** ✅

Here we are talking about a particular man.

Therefore:

> **the man**

---

## 3. Water

> **Water is essential for life.** ✅

Water is being discussed generally.

Therefore, no article.

---

## 4. Particular Water

> **The water of the river is dirty.** ✅

Here we are talking about particular water — the water of the river.

Therefore:

> **the water**

---

## 5. Gold

> **Gold is a precious metal.** ✅

Gold is being discussed generally.

No article.

---

## 6. Particular Gold

> **The gold of this ring is of inferior quality.** ✅

Here the gold is particularised by:

> **of this ring**

Therefore:

> **the gold**

---

### ⭐ Rule 51 Shortcut

| General                          | Particular                             |
| -------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| **Man** is mortal.               | I saw **the man** in the forest.       |
| **Water** is essential for life. | **The water** of the river is dirty.   |
| **Gold** is precious.            | **The gold** of this ring is inferior. |

